flowchart TB
    accTitle: How Elausys computes a price
    accDescr: The price before VAT is the product cost plus the manufacturer margin, minus the customer and site discounts added together, minus the product promotion, minus a quantity discount for professionals only. VAT then depends on the delivery: 21% in Belgium, 0% outside the EU for every customer, 0% for a professional with a valid VAT number delivered in their own EU country, and otherwise 21% or the destination country's rate.

    BASE["Cost + manufacturer margin"]
    D1["− customer + site discount<br/>added together, capped at 100%"]
    D2["− product promotion"]
    D3["− quantity discount<br/>professionals only"]
    WHERE{{"Delivered where?"}}
    BE["21% VAT"]
    OUT["0% VAT<br/>export, every customer"]
    PRO{{"Professional with a valid VAT<br/>number, in their own country?"}}
    ZERO["0% VAT<br/>reverse charge"]
    EU["21% VAT, or the<br/>destination's rate"]

    BASE --> D1 --> D2 --> D3 --> WHERE
    WHERE -->|Belgium| BE
    WHERE -->|another EU country| PRO
    WHERE -->|outside the EU| OUT
    PRO -->|yes| ZERO
    PRO -->|no| EU

    class PRO accent
